# Giocci Live: Image Demo for Offloading Computation Across the Edge, in Real Time

## Demo overview and preparation

This Livebook is an image processing demo using [Giocci](https://github.com/biyooon-ex/giocci_platform).
It displays the camera input and processing results in three columns: **Input / Local / Giocci**.
Switch between Grayscale, Edge detection, and Gaussian blur to compare total call time, kernel time, and FPS.

Set the connection details and run **Evaluate all once** to complete preparation. Press "Start" on the screen to start capturing.
After that, use the start, stop, and app controls without evaluating the cells again. Switching apps while capturing keeps the camera running. Switching apps while stopped does not start it.

This works with regular Livebook and Nerves Livebook. It uses Giocci v0.6.3.
The Livebook file is available here.

* https://github.com/biyooon-ex/nerves_livebook/blob/v0.19.0-gioccidemo/priv/giocci/giocci_live_image_demo.livemd

We assume that the Nerves firmware includes Giocci, Zenohex, Kino, StbImage, and support for the camera you use. Elixir/OTP must also be compatible with the Engine.
To build your own Nerves firmware, use the repositories and branches below. We have tested `:rpi0` (with Pi Camera) and `:rpi5` (with a USB camera).

```bash
git clone https://github.com/biyooon-ex/nerves_livebook -b v0.19.0-gioccidemo
git clone https://github.com/biyooon-ex/kiosk_system_rpi5 -b v2.0.1-gioccidemo
cd nerves_livebook
export MIX_TARGET=rpi0  # or rpi5
mix deps.get
mix firmware  # For rpi5, this takes a very long time because the system is customized for USB camera support!
mix burn  # Write the firmware to the SD card
```

In regular Livebook, install the dependencies. On Nerves, check the dependencies included in the firmware.
This is the Livebook Setup cell. It does not call Mix.install on Nerves.

```elixir
if Code.ensure_loaded?(Nerves.Runtime) do
  for module <- [Kino, Kino.Input, Giocci, Giocci.DynamicModule, StbImage] do
    unless Code.ensure_loaded?(module), do: raise("The firmware needs #{inspect(module)}")
  end
else
  Mix.install([
    {:kino, "== 0.19.1"},
    {:giocci, "== 0.6.3", runtime: false},
    {:stb_image, "~> 0.6.10"}
  ])
end
```

## 1. Connection and camera settings

Set the zenohd address, Relay name, and key_prefix for your environment.
In `endpoints`, specify a reachable IP address of the server running `zenohd`.
If you changed the Relay name, you also need to edit `relay`.

This cell configures and starts Giocci, then registers the Client with the Relay. You can check for problems with the IP address or Relay name here.
If registration fails, check the settings and network, then evaluate the cell again.
Before changing connection settings while capturing, press "Stop" first.

```elixir
# Set the zenohd address to one reachable from the Elixir runtime.
endpoints = ["tcp/127.0.0.1:7447"]
relay = "giocci_relay"
key_prefix = ""

# Automatically select the browser for regular Livebook, Pi Camera for Pi Zero, and V4L2 for Pi 5.
camera_mode = :auto
camera_device = "/dev/video0"

# Apply the connection settings, start Giocci, and check Relay registration here.
client_name = "image-demo-#{System.pid()}-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

if List.keymember?(Application.started_applications(), :giocci, 0),
  do: Application.stop(:giocci)

System.put_env("ZENOHD_CONNECT_ENDPOINTS", Enum.join(endpoints, ","))
Application.put_env(:giocci, :zenoh_config_file_path, nil)
Application.put_env(:giocci, :client_name, client_name)
Application.put_env(:giocci, :key_prefix, key_prefix)
{:ok, _} = Application.ensure_all_started(:giocci)
:ok = Giocci.register_client(relay)

IO.puts("Registered Client #{client_name} with #{relay}")
```

## 2. Define the apps and live processing

Define the three apps, timing helpers, camera capture, independent Local/Giocci processing, and browser UI.
Add `use Giocci.DynamicModule` to each app so that Giocci keeps the BEAM compiled in Livebook.

```elixir
defmodule GiocciDemo.Notebook do
  def now, do: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond)
  def ms(us), do: Float.round(us / 1000, 3)

  def check!(result, width, height, channels, tag) do
    case result do
      %{
        pixels: pixels,
        compute_us: us,
        tag: ^tag,
        width: ^width,
        height: ^height,
        channels: ^channels
      }
      when is_binary(pixels) and byte_size(pixels) == width * height * channels and
             is_integer(us) and us >= 0 ->
        result

      other ->
        raise "Invalid image-processing result: #{inspect(other, limit: 5)}"
    end
  end
end

defmodule GiocciDemo.Grayscale do
  use Giocci.DynamicModule

  def process(rgb, width, height) do
    unless width > 0 and height > 0 and byte_size(rgb) == width * height * 3,
      do: raise(ArgumentError, "invalid RGB image")

    # Approximate the weighted RGB sum with integers. The result has 1 byte per pixel.
    for <<r, g, b <- rgb>>, into: <<>> do
      <<div(77 * r + 150 * g + 29 * b, 256)>>
    end
  end

  def run(rgb, width, height, tag) do
    {us, pixels} = :timer.tc(fn -> process(rgb, width, height) end)
    %{pixels: pixels, width: width, height: height, channels: 1, compute_us: us, tag: tag}
  end
end

defmodule GiocciDemo.Sobel do
  use Giocci.DynamicModule

  def process(rgb, width, height) do
    unless width > 0 and height > 0 and byte_size(rgb) == width * height * 3,
      do: raise(ArgumentError, "invalid RGB image")

    gray = grayscale(rgb)

    for y <- 0..(height - 1), x <- 0..(width - 1), into: <<>> do
      if x == 0 or y == 0 or x == width - 1 or y == height - 1 do
        <<0>>
      else
        p = y * width + x
        a = :binary.at(gray, p - width - 1)
        b = :binary.at(gray, p - width)
        c = :binary.at(gray, p - width + 1)
        d = :binary.at(gray, p - 1)
        f = :binary.at(gray, p + 1)
        g = :binary.at(gray, p + width - 1)
        h = :binary.at(gray, p + width)
        i = :binary.at(gray, p + width + 1)
        gx = -a + c - 2 * d + 2 * f - g + i
        gy = -a - 2 * b - c + g + 2 * h + i
        # Use an L1 approximation for gradient intensity. The border is black, and intensity is capped at 255.
        <<min(255, abs(gx) + abs(gy))>>
      end
    end
  end

  # Keep this function inside the module so that save_module only needs to send this module.
  defp grayscale(rgb) do
    for <<r, g, b <- rgb>>, into: <<>>, do: <<div(77 * r + 150 * g + 29 * b, 256)>>
  end

  def run(rgb, width, height, tag) do
    # Include grayscale conversion in the Sobel processing time.
    {us, pixels} = :timer.tc(fn -> process(rgb, width, height) end)
    %{pixels: pixels, width: width, height: height, channels: 1, compute_us: us, tag: tag}
  end
end

defmodule GiocciDemo.Gaussian do
  use Giocci.DynamicModule

  @radius 8
  @sigma 4.0
  @weights for d <- -@radius..@radius, do: {d, :math.exp(-d * d / (2 * @sigma * @sigma))}
  @weight_sum Enum.reduce(@weights, 0.0, fn {_, v}, sum -> sum + v end)
  @kernel Enum.map(@weights, fn {d, v} -> {d, v / @weight_sum} end)

  def process(rgb, width, height) do
    unless width > 0 and height > 0 and byte_size(rgb) == width * height * 3,
      do: raise(ArgumentError, "invalid RGB image")

    # Use the scheduler count on the execution device. Do not create more Tasks than rows.
    concurrency = min(System.schedulers_online(), height)

    # Split the 17×17 2D convolution into horizontal and vertical passes. Blur each RGB channel separately.
    # Store intermediate results in a float64 binary to avoid rounding in the horizontal pass.
    horizontal =
      parallel_rows(height, concurrency, fn rows ->
        for y <- rows, x <- 0..(width - 1), channel <- 0..2, into: <<>> do
          value =
            Enum.reduce(@kernel, 0.0, fn {dx, weight}, sum ->
              p = (y * width + clamp(x + dx, width - 1)) * 3 + channel
              sum + weight * :binary.at(rgb, p)
            end)

          <<value::float-little-64>>
        end
      end)

    parallel_rows(height, concurrency, fn rows ->
      for y <- rows, x <- 0..(width - 1), channel <- 0..2, into: <<>> do
        value =
          Enum.reduce(@kernel, 0.0, fn {dy, weight}, sum ->
            p = (clamp(y + dy, height - 1) * width + x) * 3 + channel
            <<value::float-little-64>> = binary_part(horizontal, p * 8, 8)
            sum + weight * value
          end)

        <<clamp(round(value), 255)>>
      end
    end)
  end

  # Use edge pixels for positions outside the image (edge clamp).
  defp clamp(value, maximum), do: max(0, min(maximum, value))

  # With one scheduler, as on Pi Zero, process sequentially without creating Tasks.
  defp parallel_rows(height, 1, fun), do: fun.(0..(height - 1))

  # Process groups of rows and join the results in row order.
  # Avoid the default 5-second Task timeout on slow devices. This is separate from the Giocci timeout.
  defp parallel_rows(height, concurrency, fun) do
    chunk = div(height + concurrency - 1, concurrency)

    0..(height - 1)
    |> Enum.chunk_every(chunk)
    |> Task.async_stream(fun, max_concurrency: concurrency, ordered: true, timeout: :infinity)
    |> Enum.map(fn {:ok, binary} -> binary end)
    |> IO.iodata_to_binary()
  end

  def run(rgb, width, height, tag) do
    {us, pixels} = :timer.tc(fn -> process(rgb, width, height) end)
    %{pixels: pixels, width: width, height: height, channels: 3, compute_us: us, tag: tag}
  end
end

defmodule GiocciDemo.CameraSource do
  use GenServer, restart: :temporary

  def detect do
    if Code.ensure_loaded?(Nerves.Runtime) do
      platform =
        if Code.ensure_loaded?(Nerves.Runtime.KV),
          do: apply(Nerves.Runtime.KV, :get_active, ["nerves_fw_platform"]),
          else: nil

      model =
        case File.read("/proc/device-tree/model") do
          {:ok, value} -> String.trim_trailing(value, <<0>>)
          _ -> ""
        end

      cond do
        platform in ["rpi0", "rpi0_2"] or String.contains?(model, "Zero") -> :picamera
        platform == "rpi5" or String.contains?(model, "Raspberry Pi 5") -> :usb_v4l2
        true -> :unknown
      end
    else
      :browser
    end
  end

  def start_link(opts), do: GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts)

  @impl true
  def init(%{owner: owner, config: config}) do
    Process.flag(:trap_exit, true)

    try do
      {executable, args, layout} = command(config)

      port =
        Port.open({:spawn_executable, executable}, [
          :binary,
          :exit_status,
          :use_stdio,
          :hide,
          args: args
        ])

      send(owner, {:source_ready, self()})
      Process.send_after(self(), :sample, max(1, div(1000, config.fps)))

      {:ok,
       %{
         owner: owner,
         config: config,
         port: port,
         layout: layout,
         buffer: <<>>,
         latest: nil,
         waiting: false,
         skipped: 0
       }}
    rescue
      e -> {:stop, Exception.message(e)}
    end
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_info({port, {:data, data}}, %{port: port} = s) do
    {latest, rest, count} = take_latest(s.buffer <> data, s.layout.bytes)

    s =
      if count > 0 do
        skipped = s.skipped + count - 1 + if(s.latest == nil, do: 0, else: 1)
        %{s | buffer: rest, latest: latest, skipped: skipped}
      else
        %{s | buffer: rest}
      end

    {:noreply, s}
  end

  def handle_info(:sample, s) do
    Process.send_after(self(), :sample, max(1, div(1000, s.config.fps)))

    if s.latest != nil and not s.waiting do
      rgb = to_rgb(s.latest, s.layout, s.config.width, s.config.height)

      send(
        s.owner,
        {:camera_frame, self(), rgb, s.config.width, s.config.height, s.skipped}
      )

      {:noreply, %{s | latest: nil, waiting: true, skipped: 0}}
    else
      {:noreply, s}
    end
  end

  def handle_info(:frame_ack, s), do: {:noreply, %{s | waiting: false}}

  def handle_info({port, {:exit_status, code}}, %{port: port} = s) do
    send(s.owner, {:source_failed, self(), "Capture command exited with code #{code} (check the camera logs)"})
    {:stop, :normal, %{s | port: nil}}
  end

  def handle_info({:EXIT, port, reason}, %{port: port} = s) do
    send(s.owner, {:source_failed, self(), "Camera Port: #{inspect(reason)}"})
    {:stop, :normal, %{s | port: nil}}
  end

  def handle_info(_, s), do: {:noreply, s}

  @impl true
  def terminate(_, s), do: close_port(s.port)

  defp command(%{mode: :picamera} = c) do
    unless rem(c.width, 64) == 0 and rem(c.height, 16) == 0,
      do: raise("Pi Camera width must be a multiple of 64 and height a multiple of 16 (YUV row alignment)")

    executable =
      System.find_executable("rpicam-vid") || System.find_executable("libcamera-vid") ||
        raise("rpicam-vid / libcamera-vid not found")

    args = [
      "--nopreview",
      "--codec",
      "yuv420",
      "--flush",
      "--width",
      to_string(c.width),
      "--height",
      to_string(c.height),
      "--framerate",
      to_string(c.fps),
      "--camera",
      to_string(c.camera_index),
      "--timeout",
      "0",
      "--output",
      "-"
    ]

    {executable, args,
     %{
       format: :yuv420,
       width: c.width,
       height: c.height,
       stride: c.width,
       bytes: div(c.width * c.height * 3, 2)
     }}
  end

  defp command(%{mode: :usb_v4l2} = c) do
    executable = System.find_executable("v4l2-ctl") || raise("v4l2-ctl not found. Check the firmware")

    # Some UVC camera modes only support MJPEG. Request YUYV and check the actual settings.
    args = [
      "--device",
      c.device,
      "--set-fmt-video=width=#{c.width},height=#{c.height},pixelformat=YUYV",
      "--get-fmt-video"
    ]

    {text, status} = System.cmd(executable, args, stderr_to_stdout: true)
    unless status == 0, do: raise("Failed to configure V4L2:\n#{text}")

    unless Regex.match?(~r/Pixel Format\s*:\s*'YUYV'/, text),
      do: raise("This capture adapter requires a YUYV-compatible UVC camera:\n#{text}")

    [_, w, h] =
      Regex.run(~r/Width\/Height\s*:\s*(\d+)\/(\d+)/, text) ||
        raise("Could not read the V4L2 resolution:\n#{text}")

    w = String.to_integer(w)
    h = String.to_integer(h)
    stride = numeric_field(text, ~r/Bytes per Line\s*:\s*(\d+)/, w * 2)
    bytes = numeric_field(text, ~r/Size Image\s*:\s*(\d+)/, stride * h)

    unless w > 0 and h > 0 and rem(w, 2) == 0 and stride >= w * 2 and bytes >= stride * h and
             bytes <= 16_000_000,
           do: raise("Unexpected V4L2 frame layout:\n#{text}")

    # Even if the camera does not support setting FPS, the capture timer can limit the output rate.
    {_message, fps_status} =
      System.cmd(executable, ["--device", c.device, "--set-parm=#{c.fps}"], stderr_to_stdout: true)

    if fps_status != 0, do: IO.puts("The camera does not support setting FPS. RGB capture will be limited to #{c.fps} FPS or less")

    args = [
      "--device",
      c.device,
      "--silent",
      "--stream-mmap=3",
      "--stream-count=0",
      "--stream-to=-"
    ]

    {executable, args, %{format: :yuyv, width: w, height: h, stride: stride, bytes: bytes}}
  end

  defp numeric_field(text, regex, default) do
    case Regex.run(regex, text) do
      [_, value] -> String.to_integer(value)
      _ -> default
    end
  end

  # Port chunks and frames have different boundaries. Separate the latest complete frame from the remaining bytes.
  def take_latest(buffer, size) do
    count = div(byte_size(buffer), size)

    if count == 0 do
      {nil, buffer, 0}
    else
      latest = :binary.copy(binary_part(buffer, (count - 1) * size, size))
      rest = :binary.copy(binary_part(buffer, count * size, rem(byte_size(buffer), size)))
      {latest, rest, count}
    end
  end

  def to_rgb(raw, %{format: :yuv420} = l, width, height) do
    y_size = l.stride * l.height
    uv_stride = div(l.stride, 2)
    uv_size = div(y_size, 4)

    for y <- 0..(height - 1), x <- 0..(width - 1), into: <<>> do
      sx = div(x * l.width, width)
      sy = div(y * l.height, height)
      p = div(sy, 2) * uv_stride + div(sx, 2)

      yuv_pixel(
        :binary.at(raw, sy * l.stride + sx),
        :binary.at(raw, y_size + p),
        :binary.at(raw, y_size + uv_size + p)
      )
    end
  end

  def to_rgb(raw, %{format: :yuyv} = l, width, height) do
    for y <- 0..(height - 1), x <- 0..(width - 1), into: <<>> do
      sx = div(x * l.width, width)
      sy = div(y * l.height, height)
      p = sy * l.stride + div(sx, 2) * 4
      yuv_pixel(:binary.at(raw, p + rem(sx, 2) * 2), :binary.at(raw, p + 1), :binary.at(raw, p + 3))
    end
  end

  # BT.601 limited-range conversion for the demo. Colors may vary slightly with the camera's color space.
  defp yuv_pixel(y, u, v) do
    c = max(0, y - 16)
    d = u - 128
    e = v - 128
    clip = fn n -> max(0, min(255, div(n + 128, 256))) end
    <<clip.(298 * c + 409 * e), clip.(298 * c - 100 * d - 208 * e), clip.(298 * c + 516 * d)>>
  end

  defp close_port(nil), do: :ok

  defp close_port(port) do
    # Stop only the capture process that we started.
    case Port.info(port, :os_pid) do
      {:os_pid, pid} ->
        if kill = System.find_executable("kill"), do: System.cmd(kill, ["-TERM", to_string(pid)])

      _ ->
        :ok
    end

    try do
      Port.close(port)
    rescue
      ArgumentError -> :ok
    end
  end
end

defmodule GiocciDemo.LiveImage do
  use Kino.JS.Live

  # Use the Kino 0.19 asset format and write to a temporary directory instead of priv.
  # Prepare the archive explicitly to avoid compile-time writes by use Kino.JS.
  @js ~S"""
  export function init(ctx, initial) {
    const [config] = initial;
    const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
    canvas.width = config.width;
    canvas.height = config.height;
    canvas.style.cssText = "display:block;width:100%;height:auto;";
    const message = document.createElement("div");
    message.style.cssText = "font:12px system-ui;min-height:2.8em;overflow-wrap:anywhere;";
    ctx.root.append(canvas, message);
    const context = canvas.getContext("2d");
    const image = context.createImageData(config.width, config.height);

    function draw([info, buffer]) {
      const pixels = new Uint8Array(buffer);
      message.textContent = info.message || "";
      if (pixels.length === 0) return;
      if (info.width !== canvas.width || info.height !== canvas.height ||
          ![1, 3].includes(info.channels) ||
          pixels.length !== info.width * info.height * info.channels) return;

      // Build the next image in memory and draw it to the fixed Canvas in one step.
      // Do not erase the previous image with clearRect or by resetting the Canvas size.
      for (let src = 0, dst = 0; dst < image.data.length; dst += 4) {
        const r = pixels[src++];
        image.data[dst] = r;
        image.data[dst + 1] = info.channels === 1 ? r : pixels[src++];
        image.data[dst + 2] = info.channels === 1 ? r : pixels[src++];
        image.data[dst + 3] = 255;
      }
      context.putImageData(image, 0, 0);
    }

    ctx.handleEvent("pixels", draw);
    ctx.handleEvent("message", text => { message.textContent = text; });
    draw(initial);
  }
  """
  @hash Base.encode32(:erlang.md5(@js), case: :lower, padding: false)

  def __assets_info__ do
    path = Path.join(System.tmp_dir!(), "giocci-live-image-#{@hash}.tar.gz")
    unless File.exists?(path) do
      :ok = :erl_tar.create(path, [{~c"main.js", @js}], [:compressed])
    end
    %{archive_path: path, js_path: "main.js", hash: @hash, cdn_url: nil}
  end

  def new(width, height), do: Kino.JS.Live.new(__MODULE__, {width, height})

  def update(kino, pixels, width, height, channels) do
    Kino.JS.Live.cast(kino, {:pixels, pixels, width, height, channels})
  end

  def message(kino, text), do: Kino.JS.Live.cast(kino, {:message, text})

  @impl true
  def init({width, height}, ctx) do
    info = %{width: width, height: height, channels: 3, message: "Waiting for an image"}
    {:ok, assign(ctx, info: info, pixels: <<>>)}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_connect(ctx) do
    # Send the latest image to newly opened browsers too.
    {:ok, {:binary, ctx.assigns.info, ctx.assigns.pixels}, ctx}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_cast({:pixels, pixels, width, height, channels}, ctx) do
    info = %{width: width, height: height, channels: channels, message: ""}
    broadcast_event(ctx, "pixels", {:binary, info, pixels})
    {:noreply, assign(ctx, info: info, pixels: pixels)}
  end

  def handle_cast({:message, text}, ctx) do
    broadcast_event(ctx, "message", text)
    {:noreply, assign(ctx, info: %{ctx.assigns.info | message: text})}
  end
end

defmodule GiocciDemo.LiveCompare do
  use GenServer, restart: :temporary
  alias GiocciDemo.Notebook, as: N
  alias GiocciDemo.CameraSource
  alias GiocciDemo.LiveImage

  # Set a 30-second timeout for the Relay query and another for the Engine result.
  @remote_timeout_ms 30_000
  @work_timeout_ms 90_000
  @retry_delay_ms 10_000

  @apps %{
    grayscale: {GiocciDemo.Grayscale, 1},
    sobel: {GiocciDemo.Sobel, 1},
    gaussian: {GiocciDemo.Gaussian, 3}
  }

  def start_link(opts), do: GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts)
  def browser_start(pid, source), do: GenServer.call(pid, {:browser_start, source})
  def stop(pid), do: GenServer.cast(pid, :stop)

  @impl true
  def init(opts) do
    Process.flag(:trap_exit, true)
    Enum.each(opts.controls, fn {tag, input} -> Kino.Control.subscribe(input, tag) end)
    Process.send_after(self(), :stats, 1000)

    s =
      Map.merge(opts, %{
        running: false,
        source: nil,
        epoch: make_ref(),
        seq: 0,
        operation: :grayscale,
        started: N.now(),
        last_input: N.now(),
        inputs: [],
        source_drops: 0,
        local: lane(),
        remote: lane(),
        status: "Stopped"
      })

    {:ok, s}
  end

  defp lane do
    %{
      worker: nil, pending: nil, retry: nil, count: 0, drops: 0,
      timeouts: 0, completions: [], last: nil, failed: false
    }
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_call({:browser_start, source}, _from, s) do
    s = halt(s, "Starting browser camera")
    s = %{s | source: source, running: true, started: N.now(), last_input: N.now()}
    {:reply, :ok, %{s | status: "Running / Browser USB camera"}}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_cast(:stop, s), do: {:noreply, halt(s, "Stopped")}

  @impl true
  def handle_info({:start, _}, %{config: %{mode: :browser}} = s), do: {:noreply, s}

  def handle_info({:start, _}, s) do
    s = halt(s, "Starting camera")

    case CameraSource.start_link(%{owner: self(), config: s.config}) do
      {:ok, pid} ->
        {:noreply,
         %{s | source: pid, running: true, started: N.now(), last_input: N.now(), status: "Running"}}

      {:error, reason} ->
        {:noreply, %{s | status: "Failed to start camera: #{inspect(reason)}"}}
    end
  end

  def handle_info({:stop, _}, s), do: {:noreply, halt(s, "Stopped")}

  def handle_info({:operation, %{value: operation}}, s) when is_map_key(@apps, operation) do
    s = cancel_lanes(s)
    # Ignore completion messages from older generations in later handle_info calls.
    s = %{
      s
      | operation: operation,
        epoch: make_ref(),
        local: lane(),
        remote: lane(),
        inputs: [],
        started: N.now(),
        status: if(s.running, do: "Running", else: "Stopped")
    }

    Enum.each([s.frames.local, s.frames.remote], fn frame ->
      LiveImage.message(frame, "#{operation}: Waiting for the next result (previous image retained)")
    end)

    {:noreply, s}
  end

  def handle_info({:source_ready, source}, %{source: source} = s) do
    {:noreply, %{s | status: "Running"}}
  end

  def handle_info(
        {:camera_frame, source, rgb, width, height, drops},
        %{source: source, running: true} = s
      ) do
    valid =
      width == s.config.width and height == s.config.height and
        is_binary(rgb) and byte_size(rgb) == width * height * 3

    if valid do
      seq = s.seq + 1
      tag = {s.epoch, seq}

      frame = %{
        rgb: rgb,
        width: width,
        height: height,
        tag: tag,
        seq: seq
      }

      LiveImage.update(s.frames.input, rgb, width, height, 3)

      s = %{
        s
        | seq: seq,
          last_input: N.now(),
          inputs: [N.now() | recent(s.inputs)],
          source_drops: s.source_drops + drops
      }

      s = s |> offer(:local, frame) |> offer(:remote, frame)
      # Send one frame at a time from the browser to the runtime too. Do not wait for processing results.
      send(source, :frame_ack)
      {:noreply, s}
    else
      {:noreply, halt(s, "Invalid camera RGB frame size")}
    end
  end

  def handle_info({:source_failed, source, reason}, %{source: source} = s),
    do: {:noreply, halt(s, reason)}

  def handle_info({:completed, which, token, answer, total_us}, s) do
    current = Map.fetch!(s, which)

    case current.worker do
      %{token: ^token} = worker ->
        Process.demonitor(worker.monitor, [:flush])
        Process.cancel_timer(worker.timer)
        current = %{current | worker: nil}

        case answer do
          {:ok, result} ->
            frame = worker.frame
            now = N.now()

            LiveImage.update(
              Map.fetch!(s.frames, which),
              result.pixels, frame.width, frame.height, result.channels
            )

            last = %{
              seq: frame.seq,
              compute_us: result.compute_us,
              total_us: total_us
            }

            current = %{
              current
              | count: current.count + 1,
                completions: [now | recent(current.completions)],
                last: last
            }

            pending = current.pending
            s = Map.put(s, which, %{current | pending: nil})
            s = if s.running and pending != nil, do: launch(s, which, pending), else: s
            {:noreply, s}

          :timeout ->
            {:noreply, retry_lane(Map.put(s, which, current), which)}

          {:error, reason} ->
            {:noreply, fail_lane(Map.put(s, which, current), which, reason)}
        end

      _ ->
        {:noreply, s}
    end
  end

  def handle_info({:work_timeout, which, token}, s) do
    case Map.fetch!(s, which).worker do
      %{token: ^token} ->
        s = Map.update!(s, which, &cancel_lane/1)
        if which == :remote do
          {:noreply, retry_lane(s, which)}
        else
          {:noreply, fail_lane(s, which, "Local processing timed out. Press Stop, then Start to retry")}
        end

      _ ->
        {:noreply, s}
    end
  end

  # Keep only the latest frame while retrying. Ignore timers from before a stop or app switch.
  def handle_info({:retry_lane, which, token}, s) do
    case Map.fetch!(s, which) do
      %{retry: %{token: ^token}, pending: pending} = current when s.running ->
        s = Map.put(s, which, %{current | retry: nil, pending: nil})
        LiveImage.message(Map.fetch!(s.frames, which), "Retrying… Waiting for a result")
        {:noreply, if(pending, do: launch(s, which, pending), else: s)}

      _ ->
        {:noreply, s}
    end
  end

  def handle_info({:DOWN, monitor, :process, _pid, reason}, s) do
    s =
      Enum.reduce([:local, :remote], s, fn which, acc ->
        case Map.fetch!(acc, which).worker do
          %{monitor: ^monitor} ->
            acc = Map.update!(acc, which, &cancel_lane/1)
            fail_lane(acc, which, "Processing worker exited: #{inspect(reason)}")

          _ ->
            acc
        end
      end)

    {:noreply, s}
  end

  def handle_info({:EXIT, source, reason}, %{source: source, running: true} = s),
    do: {:noreply, halt(%{s | source: nil}, "Camera exited: #{inspect(reason)}")}

  def handle_info(:stats, s) do
    s =
      if s.running and N.now() - s.last_input > 15_000_000,
        do: halt(s, "No frames received for 15 seconds. Check the camera connection"),
        else: s

    now = N.now()
    window = min(5_000_000, max(now - s.started, 1)) / 1_000_000
    fps = fn times -> Float.round(length(recent(times)) / window, 2) end
    value = fn lane, key -> if lane.last, do: N.ms(lane.last[key]), else: "—" end
    frame_id = fn lane -> if lane.last, do: lane.last.seq, else: "—" end

    text = """
    **#{s.status}** / #{s.operation} / #{s.config.width}×#{s.config.height}

    Input FPS (RGB received): **#{fps.(s.inputs)}**

    | Metric | Local | Giocci |
    | --- | ---: | ---: |
    | Total call time (ms, latest) | #{value.(s.local, :total_us)} | #{value.(s.remote, :total_us)} |
    | Kernel time (ms, latest) | #{value.(s.local, :compute_us)} | #{value.(s.remote, :compute_us)} |
    | Result FPS (last 5 s) | #{fps.(s.local.completions)} | #{fps.(s.remote.completions)} |
    | Result frame ID | #{frame_id.(s.local)} | #{frame_id.(s.remote)} |
    | Completed frames | #{s.local.count} | #{s.remote.count} |
    | Timeouts | #{s.local.timeouts} | #{s.remote.timeouts} |
    | Frames skipped before processing | #{s.local.drops} | #{s.remote.drops} |

    Frames skipped at capture: **#{s.source_drops}**
    """

    Kino.Frame.render(s.frames.stats, Kino.Markdown.new(text), temporary: true)
    Process.send_after(self(), :stats, 1000)
    {:noreply, s}
  end

  def handle_info(_, s), do: {:noreply, s}

  defp offer(s, which, frame) do
    current = Map.fetch!(s, which)

    cond do
      current.failed ->
        s

      current.worker == nil and current.retry == nil ->
        launch(s, which, frame)

      true ->
        drops = current.drops + if(current.pending == nil, do: 0, else: 1)
        Map.put(s, which, %{current | pending: frame, drops: drops})
    end
  end

  defp launch(s, which, frame) do
    owner = self()
    token = make_ref()
    {module, channels} = Map.fetch!(@apps, s.operation)
    args = [frame.rgb, frame.width, frame.height, frame.tag]
    relay = s.relay
    # Do not wait for heavy processing or Engine queries in the UI/capture process.
    {pid, monitor} =
      :erlang.spawn_opt(
        fn ->
          {answer, call_us} =
            try do
              {call_us, result} =
                :timer.tc(fn ->
                  case which do
                    :local ->
                      apply(module, :run, args)

                    :remote ->
                      # Call the synchronous API inside a worker so the UI and Local processing do not wait.
                      case Giocci.exec_func(relay, {module, :run, args}, timeout: @remote_timeout_ms) do
                        {:error, reason} -> throw({:giocci_error, reason})
                        result -> result
                      end
                  end
                end)

              {{:ok, N.check!(result, frame.width, frame.height, channels, frame.tag)}, call_us}
            rescue
              e -> {{:error, Exception.message(e)}, nil}
            catch
              :throw, {:giocci_error, reason} ->
                answer = if timeout?(reason), do: :timeout, else: {:error, inspect(reason)}
                {answer, nil}

              :exit, {:timeout, _call} when which == :remote ->
                {:timeout, nil}

              kind, reason -> {{:error, "#{kind}: #{inspect(reason)}"}, nil}
            end

          send(owner, {:completed, which, token, answer, call_us})
        end,
        [:link, :monitor]
      )

    # Limit the total wait, including queries and result waiting inside the API. Cancel when the result arrives normally.
    timer = Process.send_after(self(), {:work_timeout, which, token}, @work_timeout_ms)

    worker = %{
      pid: pid,
      monitor: monitor,
      token: token,
      timer: timer,
      frame: frame
    }

    Map.update!(s, which, &%{&1 | worker: worker})
  end

  # Retry only known Giocci timeout formats.
  defp timeout?(:timeout), do: true
  defp timeout?({:timeout, _}), do: true
  defp timeout?("timeout"), do: true
  defp timeout?("timeout:" <> _), do: true
  defp timeout?(_), do: false

  defp retry_lane(s, which) do
    delay = @retry_delay_ms
    current = Map.fetch!(s, which)
    token = make_ref()
    timer = Process.send_after(self(), {:retry_lane, which, token}, delay)

    LiveImage.message(
      Map.fetch!(s.frames, which),
      "Retrying… Timeout ##{current.timeouts + 1}; next attempt in #{div(delay, 1000)} s"
    )

    # Do not resend the failed frame. Drop the pending image too and wait for new input.
    Map.put(s, which, %{
      current | worker: nil, pending: nil, retry: %{token: token, timer: timer},
        timeouts: current.timeouts + 1,
        drops: current.drops + if(current.pending, do: 1, else: 0)
    })
  end

  defp fail_lane(s, which, reason) do
    LiveImage.message(Map.fetch!(s.frames, which), "#{which}: Stopped / #{reason}")

    Map.update!(s, which, &%{&1 | failed: true, pending: nil})
  end

  defp recent(times) do
    cutoff = N.now() - 5_000_000
    Enum.take_while(times, &(&1 >= cutoff))
  end

  defp cancel_lane(lane) do
    if retry = lane.retry, do: Process.cancel_timer(retry.timer)

    if worker = lane.worker do
      Process.cancel_timer(worker.timer)
      Process.demonitor(worker.monitor, [:flush])
      Process.unlink(worker.pid)
      Process.exit(worker.pid, :kill)
    end

    %{lane | worker: nil, pending: nil, retry: nil}
  end

  defp cancel_lanes(s),
    do: s |> Map.update!(:local, &cancel_lane/1) |> Map.update!(:remote, &cancel_lane/1)

  defp halt(s, message) do
    if s.source && Process.alive?(s.source) do
      if s.config.mode == :browser do
        send(s.source, :stop_camera)
      else
        try do
          GenServer.stop(s.source, :normal, 5000)
        catch
          :exit, _ -> :ok
        end
      end
    end

    s = cancel_lanes(s)

    %{
      s
      | running: false,
        source: nil,
        epoch: make_ref(),
        local: lane(),
        remote: lane(),
        inputs: [],
        seq: 0,
        started: N.now(),
        source_drops: 0,
        status: message
    }
  end

  @impl true
  def terminate(_, s), do: halt(s, "Finished")
end

unless Code.ensure_loaded?(Nerves.Runtime) do
  defmodule GiocciDemo.BrowserCamera do
    use Kino.JS
    use Kino.JS.Live

    def new(controller, config), do: Kino.JS.Live.new(__MODULE__, {controller, config})

    @impl true
    def init({controller, config}, ctx) do
      Process.monitor(controller)
      {:ok, assign(ctx, controller: controller, config: config, owner: nil, session: nil)}
    end

    @impl true
    def handle_connect(ctx) do
      {:ok, Map.take(ctx.assigns.config, [:width, :height, :fps]), ctx}
    end

    @impl true
    def handle_event("start", %{"session" => session}, ctx) do
      if ctx.assigns.owner == nil do
        :ok = GiocciDemo.LiveCompare.browser_start(ctx.assigns.controller, self())
        send_event(ctx, ctx.origin, "started", %{session: session})
        {:noreply, assign(ctx, owner: ctx.origin, session: session)}
      else
        send_event(ctx, ctx.origin, "rejected", %{message: "Another camera session is running. Stop it first."})
        {:noreply, ctx}
      end
    end

    def handle_event("frame", {:binary, info, rgb}, ctx) do
      c = ctx.assigns.config

      if ctx.origin == ctx.assigns.owner and info["session"] == ctx.assigns.session and
           byte_size(rgb) == c.width * c.height * 3 do
        send(
          ctx.assigns.controller,
          {:camera_frame, self(), rgb, c.width, c.height, 0}
        )
      end

      {:noreply, ctx}
    end

    def handle_event("stop", %{"session" => session}, ctx) do
      if ctx.origin == ctx.assigns.owner and session == ctx.assigns.session do
        GiocciDemo.LiveCompare.stop(ctx.assigns.controller)
      end

      {:noreply, ctx}
    end

    @impl true
    def handle_info(:frame_ack, ctx) do
      if ctx.assigns.owner,
        do: send_event(ctx, ctx.assigns.owner, "ack", %{session: ctx.assigns.session})

      {:noreply, ctx}
    end

    def handle_info(:stop_camera, ctx) do
      if ctx.assigns.owner,
        do: send_event(ctx, ctx.assigns.owner, "stop", %{session: ctx.assigns.session})

      {:noreply, assign(ctx, owner: nil, session: nil)}
    end

    def handle_info({:DOWN, _, :process, _, _}, ctx) do
      broadcast_event(ctx, "shutdown", %{})
      {:noreply, assign(ctx, owner: nil, session: nil)}
    end

    asset "main.js" do
      ~S"""
      export function init(ctx, config) {
        ctx.root.innerHTML = `
          <div style="font:14px system-ui;display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
            <select aria-label="Select USB camera"></select>
            <button class="start">Start browser camera</button>
            <button class="stop" disabled>Stop</button>
            <span class="status">Select a USB camera</span>
            <video muted playsinline style="display:none"></video>
          </div>`;
        const select = ctx.root.querySelector('select');
        const start = ctx.root.querySelector('.start');
        const stop = ctx.root.querySelector('.stop');
        const status = ctx.root.querySelector('.status');
        const video = ctx.root.querySelector('video');
        const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
        canvas.width = config.width; canvas.height = config.height;
        const drawing = canvas.getContext('2d', {willReadFrequently: true});
        let stream = null, timer = null, watchdog = null, active = false, session = null, sequence = 0;

        async function devices(preferred) {
          const list = await navigator.mediaDevices.enumerateDevices();
          const selected = preferred || select.value;
          select.replaceChildren(new Option('Auto (select a USB camera recommended)', ''));
          list.filter(d => d.kind === 'videoinput').forEach((d, i) => {
            select.add(new Option(d.label || `Camera ${i + 1}`, d.deviceId));
          });
          if ([...select.options].some(o => o.value === selected)) select.value = selected;
        }

        function cleanup(notify = true) {
          clearTimeout(timer); clearTimeout(watchdog);
          if (notify && session) ctx.pushEvent('stop', {session});
          if (stream) stream.getTracks().forEach(t => t.stop());
          stream = null; video.srcObject = null; active = false;
          start.disabled = false; stop.disabled = true; select.disabled = false;
          status.textContent = 'Stopped';
          session = null;
        }

        function sample() {
          if (!active || !stream) return;
          // Keep the aspect ratio and use black padding. Use the same RGB for the input and both execution destinations.
          drawing.fillStyle = '#000'; drawing.fillRect(0, 0, config.width, config.height);
          const scale = Math.min(config.width / video.videoWidth, config.height / video.videoHeight);
          const w = Math.round(video.videoWidth * scale), h = Math.round(video.videoHeight * scale);
          drawing.drawImage(video, Math.floor((config.width - w) / 2), Math.floor((config.height - h) / 2), w, h);
          const rgba = drawing.getImageData(0, 0, config.width, config.height).data;
          const rgb = new Uint8Array(config.width * config.height * 3);
          for (let i = 0, j = 0; i < rgba.length; i += 4) {
            rgb[j++] = rgba[i]; rgb[j++] = rgba[i+1]; rgb[j++] = rgba[i+2];
          }
          ctx.pushEvent('frame', [{session}, rgb.buffer]);
          // Wait for ACK before sending the next frame. Do not accumulate arrays during communication.
          watchdog = setTimeout(() => { cleanup(); status.textContent += ' / No response from runtime'; }, 15000);
        }

        start.onclick = async () => {
          if (stream || active) return;
          start.disabled = true; select.disabled = true;
          const requestedSession = String(++sequence);
          session = requestedSession;
          try {
            if (!window.isSecureContext || !navigator.mediaDevices?.getUserMedia)
              throw new Error('Open Livebook via localhost or HTTPS');
            const deviceId = select.value;
            const acquired = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({audio: false, video: {
              width: {ideal: config.width}, height: {ideal: config.height},
              ...(deviceId ? {deviceId: {exact: deviceId}} : {})
            }});
            // Release the camera even if the cell is removed or stopped while the permission dialog is open.
            if (session !== requestedSession || !ctx.root.isConnected) {
              acquired.getTracks().forEach(t => t.stop()); return;
            }
            stream = acquired; video.srcObject = stream; await video.play();
            await devices(stream.getVideoTracks()[0].getSettings().deviceId);
            stop.disabled = false;
            ctx.pushEvent('start', {session});
            watchdog = setTimeout(() => { cleanup(); status.textContent += ' / No response to start request'; }, 15000);
          } catch (e) {
            cleanup(); status.textContent += ` / ${e.message}`;
          }
        };
        stop.onclick = () => cleanup();
        ctx.handleEvent('started', data => {
          if (data.session !== session) return;
          clearTimeout(watchdog); active = true;
          status.textContent = `Capturing / ${config.width}×${config.height}`;
          sample();
        });
        ctx.handleEvent('ack', data => {
          if (!active || data.session !== session) return;
          clearTimeout(watchdog); timer = setTimeout(sample, 1000 / config.fps);
        });
        ctx.handleEvent('stop', data => { if (data.session === session) cleanup(false); });
        ctx.handleEvent('rejected', data => { cleanup(false); status.textContent += ` / ${data.message}`; });
        ctx.handleEvent('shutdown', () => cleanup(false));
        window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => cleanup());
        // Stop when the embedded area is removed too. pagehide handles full-page navigation.
        const observer = new MutationObserver(() => {
          if (!ctx.root.isConnected) { cleanup(); observer.disconnect(); }
        });
        observer.observe(document.documentElement, {childList: true, subtree: true});
        if (navigator.mediaDevices?.enumerateDevices) devices().catch(() => {});
      }
      """
    end
  end
end
```

## 3. Distribute the apps and prepare the display

Use the Client registered in "1. Connection and camera settings" to distribute each of the three apps with save_module and display the controls.
Once ready, press "Start" on Nerves. In regular Livebook, select a browser camera and start it.
You do not need to evaluate this cell again when starting, stopping, or switching apps.
Before changing settings or filter code, stop first, then evaluate the changed cell and the following cells again.

```elixir
# Distribute the BEAM kept by use Giocci.DynamicModule using only the module name.
for module <- [GiocciDemo.Grayscale, GiocciDemo.Sobel, GiocciDemo.Gaussian] do
  :ok = Giocci.save_module(relay, module)
end

# You can select :auto / :browser (regular Livebook) / :picamera / :usb_v4l2.
detected_mode = GiocciDemo.CameraSource.detect()
camera_mode = if camera_mode == :auto, do: detected_mode, else: camera_mode

unless camera_mode in [:browser, :picamera, :usb_v4l2],
  do: raise("Cannot detect the input source. Set camera_mode explicitly")

if camera_mode == :browser and Code.ensure_loaded?(Nerves.Runtime),
  do: raise("On Nerves, select :picamera or :usb_v4l2")

# Use a fixed image size for the live comparison. Use a smaller size on Pi Zero to reduce the load.
{live_width, live_height, input_fps} =
  if camera_mode == :picamera, do: {192, 128, 5}, else: {320, 240, 10}

camera_config = %{
  mode: camera_mode,
  width: live_width,
  height: live_height,
  fps: input_fps,
  device: camera_device,
  camera_index: 0
}

# When this cell is evaluated again, Kino stops the old controller and releases the camera and workers too.
operation_control =
  Kino.Input.select("App", grayscale: "Grayscale", sobel: "Edge detection", gaussian: "Gaussian blur")

start_control = Kino.Control.button("Start (Nerves camera)")
stop_control = Kino.Control.button("Stop")

frames = %{
  input: GiocciDemo.LiveImage.new(live_width, live_height),
  local: GiocciDemo.LiveImage.new(live_width, live_height),
  remote: GiocciDemo.LiveImage.new(live_width, live_height),
  stats: Kino.Frame.new()
}

{:ok, live_pid} =
  Kino.start_child(
    {GiocciDemo.LiveCompare,
     %{
       config: camera_config,
       relay: relay,
       frames: frames,
       controls: [start: start_control, stop: stop_control, operation: operation_control]
     }}
  )

Kino.render(
  Kino.Markdown.new("**Input: #{camera_mode} / #{live_width}×#{live_height} / Requested limit: #{input_fps} FPS**")
)

Kino.render(operation_control)

if camera_mode == :browser do
  Kino.render(GiocciDemo.BrowserCamera.new(live_pid, camera_config))
  Kino.render(stop_control)
else
  Kino.render(Kino.Layout.grid([start_control, stop_control], columns: 2))
end

Kino.render(
  Kino.Layout.grid(
    for {title, frame} <- [{"Input", frames.input}, {"Local", frames.local}, {"Giocci", frames.remote}] do
      Kino.Layout.grid([Kino.Markdown.new("**#{title}**"), frame])
    end,
    columns: 3
  )
)

Kino.render(frames.stats)

:ok
```

## Trouble shooting

Check that Zenohd is running, that the IP address in `endpoints` is correct, and that the Relay and Engine are running correctly.
You can also find explanations in [giocci_live_handson.livemd](https://github.com/biyooon-ex/nerves_livebook/blob/v0.19.0-gioccidemo/priv/giocci/giocci_live_handson.livemd).

You can find me on the Elixir, Nerves, and AtomVM Discord servers! I am also in the Elixir, Erlang, and EEF Slack Workspaces. If you have any trouble, please contact `@takasehideki`!
